WEBVTT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.140
Welcome!

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.450
<i>My name is Masuda, 24 years old.</i>

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>I've worked various part time 
jobs for three years.</i>

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.210
<i>My dream is to become a comedian.</i>

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:20.230
<b>Masuda-kun (24)</b>

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.840
<i>I started this job to save up money</i>

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.580
<i>to go to a comedian training school,</i>

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.600
<i>but I was recognized for my exemplary work,</i>

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>and was asked by the regional manager 
to become this store's manager.</i>

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.580
Thank you.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.760
<i>When I told my girlfriend, 
who lives with me</i>

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.840
<i>(30 years of age, helps with 
chores at home), she said,</i>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.170
<i>"It's been over a month since 
my last one came."</i>

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.180
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.540
<i>I'm Masuda-kun on the brink!</i>

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.600
Fundoshi!

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.720
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.720
<b>Episode 11
"Muromi-san and the Chill"</b>

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.070
<i>It was hot.</i>

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.030
<i>It was a really hot day.</i>

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.980
<i>The heat hung over my head,</i>

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.510
<i>making me believe that</i>

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.770
<i>the sun might have even 
fallen from the sky.</i>

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.580
<i>Summer.</i>

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.000
<i>People expect a lot of it.</i>

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.520
<i>They believe that something might happen,</i>

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.150
<i>that something might change.</i>

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.760
<i>That's what I thought when I felt that heat,</i>

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.050
<i>and then I realized,</i>

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.860
<i>all of that was nothing 
more than a mirage.</i>

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.260
<b>Popsicles</b>

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.260
Excuse me. I'll take a popsicle.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:45.470
200 yen.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.270
200 yen.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.520
Otohime-san.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.320
You quit the fishing goods store?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.840
Is it bad for me to work other jobs 
when I don't have a shift there?

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.070
I didn't say that.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.320
It must be pretty difficult to 
work in this ridiculous heat.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.200
Not really.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.530
You guys are just too used 
to your air conditioning.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.590
Do you really need the money that badly?

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.500
Yes.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.880
I will stand on the top once again.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.000
You're going to build another Ryuuguujou?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.230
That's only my final goal.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.910
My current goal is...

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.010
Is...?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:21.940
To rule over the land!

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:22.590
What?!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.100
Rule the land!

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.510
I want you to work on land, too!

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.510
<i>You're selling popsicles. 
What are you saying?</i>

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.260
Aren't part time jobs a 
slow way to make money?

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.500
I'd imagine that stocks and investing

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.830
would get you money faster.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.430
<b>Not that I know these things.</b>

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.360
I tried that already.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.660
I lost the small amount of money

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.050
I had when I first came on 
land to the Great Depression,

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.650
and after that, I lost 
my hard-earned capital

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.030
to Black Monday and the American dollar.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.340
When I put money I earned during the 
bubble economy into Wall Street,

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:50.250
<b>Market Crash</b>

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:50.250
<b>Down 3,836 points 
Greatest drop in history</b>

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.250
that was when Lehman Brothers went under!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.210
<b>How about some risk management?</b>

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.210
I'm sorry.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.000
But I'm amazed.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.310
Most people usually break when 
they hit so many failures.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.920
I can't break here.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.140
My pride is on the line!

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.060
I won't let this end with those monster 
fish making a fool out of me!

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.930
<i>Muromi-san, again?</i>

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.220
How sad.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.520
So the famous Ryuuguujou has gone under.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.970
Maybe it's just deserts for your

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.550
underhanded methods of making money.

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:18.960
I guess you never learned the meaning

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.480
of "all good things come to an end."

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:24.200
This is why I'm here in shame, 
asking for your assistance.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.730
Not happening.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.130
There's no benefit to us for helping you.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.200
No one in the sea believes 
anything you say.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:33.910
Fine! Just watch me!

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.460
If I don't have the sea, 
I still have the land!

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.690
Once I have the land firmly in my 
hands, I'll come to rule the sea,

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.420
and watch as I bring you all to tears!

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.370
Tears?!

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.290
You mean like you are right now?

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.360
Everyone, point at the 
pitiful woman and laugh!

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.310
It was the first time I was made to 
experience such agony and frustration.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.820
I swore I wouldn't return to the sea

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.430
until I could make those 
monster fish admit

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.100
they were wrong and 
stand high above them.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.820
<i>The only thing pushing Otohime-san 
further right now is 100% hatred.</i>

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:05.010
Wait, so Muromi-san isn't 
involved in what happened here?

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:05.940
Muromi?

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.360
You mean the girl from before?

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:10.030
She actually helped business out.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.150
She was a good customer.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.000
I see.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:17.900
You've got one chance! One chance!

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.900
No! Oh! No way!

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.270
She knew a lot of humans as well,

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.230
so she'd bring in a lot of 
newly-made millionaires,

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.460
and then send them home penniless.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.050
There is no shame in a gambler 
going broke by gambling.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.750
They still wouldn't hate her after that.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.050
She's a strange girl.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.370
It looks like she believes the false rumors

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:27.910
that the other monster 
fish started spreading

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.910
after the Ryuuguujou went under.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.600
If she's mistaken, you should just tell her.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.420
You can only clear up 
misunderstandings through action.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:42.650
No matter what you say, it'll 
only come off as an excuse.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.270
You think I could get another?

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.380
Don't blame me if you get a stomachache.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.530
Here you go.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:55.950
Huh?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.020
A present.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.540
Good luck with work.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.660
Pretty cheeky for a kid.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.600
Takkun, did you know 
this actor and actress

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.110
are, like, seconds away 
from getting married?!

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:16.060
You know it's not good to trust 
things with no evidence at all.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.060
Muromi-san.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.770
So summer's coming to an end again.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:27.820
I should be happy to see fall coming, 
with all its good food to harvest,

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.730
and even so I'm in low spirits.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.120
I wonder if it's because I was 
corrupted by the ocean for so long.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.950
Then how about coming back?

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:38.100
Get lost, loser.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:38.660
Ouch.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.540
Don't just dillydally around here!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.170
Help with cleaning the infestation of jellyfish

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.840
in the Yellow Sea like you're supposed to!

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.050
Too tight!

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.810
This attack works well, doesn't it?

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.930
You fish sure do get along well.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:54.180
You monster fish shouldn't be 
showing your faces on the surface!

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.100
Well, well, if it isn't our fallen noble.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.520
You look even poorer 
than you did last time.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.970
Looks like you're not getting 
any results up there on land!

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.070
You planning on rotting 
away up there forever?

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:07.540
Shut up, monster fish!

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:09.980
Time moves faster here than underwater.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:13.030
I'm currently preparing for 
the trends that are to come!

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.290
You're really reaching 
with your excuses now.

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.160
How many years has it been now?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.750
If you're fighting like 
that all the time,

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.460
you'll never really talk things over.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:24.780
What, Takkun?!

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.480
You're taking the side of this evil wench?!

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.160
<b>That was mean!</b>

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.920
I just want you to calm down a bit.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.790
Why don't you be a good fish 
and get turned into sushi?

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.150
Then I'll just taste even better!

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:39.100
Wait just a second, Otohime-san!

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.920
Oh man, she's gone.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.020
Do you hate Otohime-san that much?

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.520
Why are you worrying about 
a girl like that anyway?

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.170
<i>You can only clear up 
misunderstandings through action.</i>

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.110
<i>No matter what you say, it'll 
only come off as an excuse.</i>

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.730
<i>Maybe an outsider can't really 
butt into this sort of thing.</i>

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:00.580
Well, it's not like we're strangers...

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.980
I liked the Ryuuguujou.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:08.550
Huh?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.680
I'm just kind of frustrated it's 
taking so long to come back.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.880
It seems like she really wants 
to make another Ryuuguujou,

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.300
so if you want her to, why 
not just let her know?

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:22.520
I liked the Ryuuguujou, but I 
couldn't care less about Otohime.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:28.550
But, if she's not there to run it...

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:32.950
I see, so it's not like the two 
of you hate each other, but...

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.160
They're both just not being 
honest with each other.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.620
I told you to get back to work!

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.580
You're going to break my sternum!

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:42.690
It started raining because of you!

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:47.550
<i>For all her abusive yelling, maybe 
Otohime-san actually understands.</i>

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:53.070
Monster fish... How shall I 
cook you once I succeed?

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.720
<i>No, she really seems 
like she hates them.</i>

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.720
Muromi-san...

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.140
It's still pretty hot, even 
though summer's ending.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.060
It's like heaven inside 
these convenience stores.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:09.480
<i>At least there was a time 
when I used to believe that.</i>

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.880
It's a curry flavored Karikari-kun.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:14.390
<b>Karikari-kun 
Curry flavor</b>

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.400
I love these.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.140
Levia-san, what are you doing?!

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.160
Oh, Takkun.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.950
I'm out shopping.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.620
If you want something, I'll buy it for you.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.080
No, I'll buy my own stuff.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:25.450
Oh, well.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.000
Hey, Masuda-kun. Throw in a 
chili-flavored fried chicken.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.770
Hey, don't just call him "-kun" like that...

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.000
Oh, she comes here all the time.

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:35.130
Levia-san always buys a bunch of stuff.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:36.090
Yup.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.920
You come up to land to buy stuff a lot?

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:41.810
The products change out 
pretty often, so it's fun.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.520
This Chu-Hi is even cheaper than water.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.390
<b>The power of corporations</b>

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.390
You're gonna buy more?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.440
You're young, so feel free 
to let me get you something.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.100
No, I'm—

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.120
Hey, there's people behind you.

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.320
Hurry up.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:52.360
<i>Otohime-san?</i>

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:53.400
<i>Otohime-san?</i>

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.650
<i>Otohime-san?!</i>

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.650
<b>Kimchi</b>

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.650
<b>Liquor</b>

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:55.860
Liquor with your dinner?

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.250
Some nights I want to drink, you know?

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:58.360
Sounds lonely.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.570
Oto-chan, Oto-chan!

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:03.050
Don't drink by yourself. 
Drink with me.

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:06.040
I never would have thought I'd get 
an invitation from a giant sea monster.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.500
<i>Levia-san and Otohime-san together...</i>

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.550
Do the two of you know each other?

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:11.450
Yeah.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.440
I lived in the sea before.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:17.050
There's no true sea-dweller 
who doesn't know Levia-san.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.400
Really?

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.330
I know most of what goes 
on in the sea as well.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.770
Muromi has told me what you've been

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:24.480
up to since you left the sea,

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:26.310
but it doesn't seem like 
things are going well.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.250
How about giving up?

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.870
I don't have that luxury.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:34.820
The day I give up will be the day 
I disappear from this world.

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:38.110
Tell me when that day comes, then.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.340
<i>What's with that exchange just now?</i>

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.950
<i>It feels like both were casually saying 
some pretty serious stuff.</i>

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:45.910
Levia-san!

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.250
I heard you were going to have a junk 
food party at the convenience store.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.130
<i>Now the conversation's 
going to go even worse.</i>

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.130
<b>Ugh...</b>

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.470
Huh? What?

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.790
Otohime's here too.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.340
I just kinda ran into her.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.800
I'm going home!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.260
I have no desire to hang 
out with some fish!

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:01.180
Don't say that.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.640
Have a drink with me first.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:04.530
Ow! Fine, just let go!

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.300
Look at how all these 
large corporations

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:08.950
have their products in even 
a small convenience store.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:12.240
No matter how much you try, you'll 
never become a big player on land.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.020
There's room to make a name for myself.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:17.740
Fluctuations in the economy can lead 
to a chance for entrepreneurs.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.700
Okay, how about we start with 
the cheap beer knockoffs?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:21.450
You want some too, Takkun?

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.380
I'm underage.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.390
I never thought they'd 
be here until morning.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.120
I need to hurry and clean up.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.490
Thanks.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.770
<i>And before the sun had risen very far,</i>

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:36.120
<i>that one dreamlike night 
with all of them together</i>

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.750
<i>had faded, leaving nothing behind.</i>

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.410
<i>No matter the dream, there comes a 
time when we must wake up from it.</i>

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:46.000
<b>We're still going!</b>

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.700
<i>That time may be closer than we think.</i>

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.130
<b>See you next week!</b>

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:48.640
<i>I pray that you have sweet dreams.</i>

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.480
It feels like my chest is hot!

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.760
What's wrong, Fuji-san? 
Did you drink too much?

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.070
My heart's beating quick.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:54.660
Arrhythmia?

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:56.340
My heart swings like a pendulum.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:57.890
No surprise, as big as yours are.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:11:58.650
Like "boing," right?

00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:59.800
Is this koi (love)?!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.070
They've got big attitudes for 
